# Report: Lease source-authority regression tests (Architect post-epic ruling, item 2)

Only one test was new. The other two acceptance items already had tests, and I confirmed with mutations that those tests catch the failure they guard against. The change is tests only: `git diff -- src` is empty, and nothing is staged or committed. I didn't touch the yin.repl files, main_test.cljc or orchestrator-log.md.

Changed: `test/dao/lease_composition_test.cljc` (+28 lines, one deftest).

## Acceptance items

| # | Invariant | Status | Test |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | A judge can wire and read its own grantor-authored medium | **Partly covered before; now fully covered (NEW test)** | `a-judge-wires-and-reads-its-own-grantor-authored-medium-test` |
| 2 | remote-serve refuses an inbound medium with `:source` = `::grantor` | **Already covered** | `open-refuses-each-missing-or-malformed-lease-option`, the testing block at `test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve_test.cljc:407` |
| 3 | Renewal media remain attributed to their holder | **Already covered** | `serving-grants-a-lease-to-a-served-renewal-medium` (`test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve_test.cljc:735`) |

**Item 1:** `grantor-authored-facts-establish-terms-test` (`test/dao/lease_test.cljc:1398`) already checked that a `:grantor`-sourced fact seeds tenure. But it works at the `initial-judge`/`wire-facts` level. No test built the judge through `make-judge` or `wire-declared-facts`, which is where the ruling says a blanket refusal must not be added. The medium at line 115 that the ruling cites is the holder's medium, not the judge's.

The new test builds a `:self :grantor` judge with a `:source :grantor` ledger medium, once through each API. It checks that both paths wire the medium. It then appends a grantor grant to that ledger and checks that each judge seeds tenure with the grant's holder.

## Mutations (each reverted)

| Mutation | Result |
|---|---|
| A. `make-judge` and `wire-declared-facts` refuse a medium whose `:source` equals the judge's own `:self` | **Only the new test fails.** No other test caught this. The new test still fails with just the `wire-declared-facts` half. |
| B. `resolve-author` silently returns nil for self-sourced media | The new test fails on both paths, and so do two existing `lease_test` tests. |
| C. `claims-grantor?` always returns false (the grantor-source guard is removed) | The item 2 test fails (lines 414, 415, 417). |
| D. The renewal medium is wired with `:source grantor` instead of the holder's identity | The item 3 test fails at line 735, and so do the renewal, release and detach end-to-end tests (17 failures, 1 error). |

